<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation (Gallus gallus / Mus musculus tetrapod autopod digits & synovial joint interzones)",
        "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation faithfully reproduces Gallus gallus / Mus musculus tetrapod autopod digits & synovial joint interzones morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gallus gallus / Mus musculus tetrapod autopod digits & synovial joint interzones specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-joint-interzone-clefting-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py> ;
    schema:about "Gallus gallus / Mus musculus tetrapod autopod digits & synovial joint interzones" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A full Biot u-p or triphasic solution, 3D geometry, synovial fluid flow, capsule/ligament mechanics, convex-head emergence from growth (the model's head contour is flat because the lens cancels the arch), or any dimensional embryonic poroelastic constant",
        "reconstructed_in_script: GDF5-Noggin 2x2 Turing dispersion with D=0 control; 1D growing-domain RD PDE with a distal PFR mask; 2D digit-ray view; Kavanagh 12-taxon morphospace regression; six genetic/signalling perturbations; radiograph segmentation of Digits II-IV",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: reduced 2D Biot storage-equation cavitation solver (HA synthesis -> osmotic pore pressure with free drainage -> cohesion threshold -> irreversible cavity phase field), three literature cavitation conditions, muscle-loading and permeability sweeps, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion, and the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord comparison",
        "reported_in_source: Drachman & Sokoloff (1966), Kahn et al. (2009): paralysed or muscle-less embryos specify interzones but fail to cavitate and the interzone re-chondrifies; Roddy et al. (2011): immobilised rudiments lose articular curvature",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards et al. (1994), Dowthwaite et al. (1998): cavitation coincides with mechanosensitive hyaluronan accumulation and loss of interzone cohesion; Mow et al. (1980), Maroudas (1976): cartilage is a biphasic poroelastic solid whose Donnan swelling pressure is ~0.1-0.25 MPa",
        "reported_in_source: Hiscock et al. (2017), Hartmann & Tabin (2001): periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ interzones segment a chondrogenic digit ray; Brunet et al. (1998): Nog-/- embryos form no joints; Storm et al. (1994): Gdf5 bp/bp fuses interphalangeal joints",
        "reported_in_source: Kavanagh et al. (2013): phalanx lengths of triphalangeal digits across tetrapods fall on the inhibitory-cascade line P2/P1 = 1/2 + 1/2 (P3/P1), i.e. P2 is 1/3 of the phalangeal total",
        "transfer_boundary: The 1D RD PDE does not self-organise its joint positions: `joint_targets` are pre-computed from the arithmetic progression and injected as a Gaussian source behind the PFR, and the bp/bp PIP fusion is hard-coded (L334-349, L364-373); the Turing dispersion is verified analytically, not as the pattern-selecting mechanism of the PDE",
        "transfer_boundary: The poroelastic solver has a rigid solid skeleton (no u-p Biot displacement, effective stress, capsule or ligament), is 2D, one-way coupled (RD -> poroelastic), and its articular arch is a parametric Carter-Wong rule a(y) = A_arc phi(m)(1 - (y/W)^2), not a computed growth response; all constants are dimensionless and scaled only to adult cartilage",
        "transfer_boundary: The vendored specimen is a juvenile hand radiograph with open physes, not an embryonic interzone section; the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd > mean" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py; output: docs/media/joint_interzone_clefting_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus / Mus musculus tetrapod autopod digits & synovial joint interzones; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 1d288d48a8d6a46b269ac8c181dfcb21e621b3dfef13912fa8b3a56d847f9a0e; artifact_sha256: 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/joint_interzone_clefting_reference.json=8ce3cc464602a827..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/paper_citations.bib=4dba5970a1ffae76..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/scout_manifest.json=1ae24e293d2062b2..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/synovial_cavitation_reference.json=9ca273ead3e3606e..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/tetrapod_digit_interzone_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-joint-interzone-clefting-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kavanagh et al. (2013): phalanx lengths of triphalangeal digits across tetrapods fall on the inhibitory-cascade line P2/P1 = 1/2 + 1/2 (P3/P1), i.e. P2 is 1/3 of the phalangeal total | Hiscock et al. (2017), Hartmann & Tabin (2001): periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ interzones segment a chondrogenic digit ray; Brunet et al. (1998): Nog-/- embryos form no joints; Storm et al. (1994): Gdf5 bp/bp fuses interphalangeal joints | Drachman & Sokoloff (1966), Kahn et al. (2009): paralysed or muscle-less embryos specify interzones but fail to cavitate and the interzone re-chondrifies; Roddy et al. (2011): immobilised rudiments lose articular curvature | Edwards et al. (1994), Dowthwaite et al. (1998): cavitation coincides with mechanosensitive hyaluronan accumulation and loss of interzone cohesion; Mow et al. (1980), Maroudas (1976): cartilage is a biphasic poroelastic solid whose Donnan swelling pressure is ~0.1-0.25 MPa; reconstructed_in_script: GDF5-Noggin 2x2 Turing dispersion with D=0 control; 1D growing-domain RD PDE with a distal PFR mask; 2D digit-ray view; Kavanagh 12-taxon morphospace regression; six genetic/signalling perturbations; radiograph segmentation of Digits II-IV | Pass 3: reduced 2D Biot storage-equation cavitation solver (HA synthesis -> osmotic pore pressure with free drainage -> cohesion threshold -> irreversible cavity phase field), three literature cavitation conditions, muscle-loading and permeability sweeps, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion, and the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord comparison; transfer_boundary: The 1D RD PDE does not self-organise its joint positions: `joint_targets` are pre-computed from the arithmetic progression and injected as a Gaussian source behind the PFR, and the bp/bp PIP fusion is hard-coded (L334-349, L364-373); the Turing dispersion is verified analytically, not as the pattern-selecting mechanism of the PDE | The poroelastic solver has a rigid solid skeleton (no u-p Biot displacement, effective stress, capsule or ligament), is 2D, one-way coupled (RD -> poroelastic), and its articular arch is a parametric Carter-Wong rule a(y) = A_arc phi(m)(1 - (y/W)^2), not a computed growth response; all constants are dimensionless and scaled only to adult cartilage | The vendored specimen is a juvenile hand radiograph with open physes, not an embryonic interzone section; the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd > mean; does_not_claim: A full Biot u-p or triphasic solution, 3D geometry, synovial fluid flow, capsule/ligament mechanics, convex-head emergence from growth (the model's head contour is flat because the lens cancels the arch), or any dimensional embryonic poroelastic constant]; other sources: The formation of human synovial joint cavities: a possible role for hyaluronan and CD44 in altered interzone cohesion <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7961140/>" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
