<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — MorphoEval overall 89.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) re-scored evaluation of `2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py` (overall weighted score 89.4/100, down 7.2 from the v2 score of 96.6). The single v2 remediation item is closed: the 2D Gdf5 interzone field now drives a reduced Biot poroelastic cavitation solver (hyaluronan synthesis, Donnan osmotic pore pressure with Darcy drainage, HA/CD44 loss of cohesion, irreversible cavity phase field, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion) that reproduces the three literature outcomes (motile WT 3 interzones -> 3 cavities; paralysed 3 -> 0 with interzone Sox9 0.81 vs 0.23; Nog-/- 0 -> 0), has monotone muscle-loading (m* = 0.80) and permeability sweeps, matches the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord (0.064 vs 0.056 +/- 0.078; 3/4 joints convex-head sign), and is backed by two new machine-verified Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys). Scoring the current file line by line, however, exposed defects that v2 did not deduct for: templated joint positions and hard-coded PIP fusion in the RD PDE, an imposed rather than emergent articular arch (the modelled head contour is flat), a juvenile specimen with a low-contrast Digit II centerline and a hard-coded cleft count, and several uncited Pass 3 calibration constants. These are carried as 8 line-pinned Pass 4 items. Overall 89.4/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 94.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 96, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/joint_interzone_clefting_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py at d58a084, image/png, 1021079 B, 2610×1566 px, artifact_sha256 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5 (sha256 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5), spec_fingerprint 1d288d48a8d6a46b269ac8c181dfcb21e621b3dfef13912fa8b3a56d847f9a0e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1d288d48a8d6a46b269ac8c181dfcb21e621b3dfef13912fa8b3a56d847f9a0e; artifact_sha256: 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/joint_interzone_clefting_reference.json=8ce3cc464602a827..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/paper_citations.bib=4dba5970a1ffae76..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/scout_manifest.json=1ae24e293d2062b2..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/synovial_cavitation_reference.json=9ca273ead3e3606e..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/tetrapod_digit_interzone_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-joint-interzone-clefting-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kavanagh et al. (2013): phalanx lengths of triphalangeal digits across tetrapods fall on the inhibitory-cascade line P2/P1 = 1/2 + 1/2 (P3/P1), i.e. P2 is 1/3 of the phalangeal total | Hiscock et al. (2017), Hartmann & Tabin (2001): periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ interzones segment a chondrogenic digit ray; Brunet et al. (1998): Nog-/- embryos form no joints; Storm et al. (1994): Gdf5 bp/bp fuses interphalangeal joints | Drachman & Sokoloff (1966), Kahn et al. (2009): paralysed or muscle-less embryos specify interzones but fail to cavitate and the interzone re-chondrifies; Roddy et al. (2011): immobilised rudiments lose articular curvature | Edwards et al. (1994), Dowthwaite et al. (1998): cavitation coincides with mechanosensitive hyaluronan accumulation and loss of interzone cohesion; Mow et al. (1980), Maroudas (1976): cartilage is a biphasic poroelastic solid whose Donnan swelling pressure is ~0.1-0.25 MPa; reconstructed_in_script: GDF5-Noggin 2x2 Turing dispersion with D=0 control; 1D growing-domain RD PDE with a distal PFR mask; 2D digit-ray view; Kavanagh 12-taxon morphospace regression; six genetic/signalling perturbations; radiograph segmentation of Digits II-IV | Pass 3: reduced 2D Biot storage-equation cavitation solver (HA synthesis -> osmotic pore pressure with free drainage -> cohesion threshold -> irreversible cavity phase field), three literature cavitation conditions, muscle-loading and permeability sweeps, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion, and the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord comparison; transfer_boundary: The 1D RD PDE does not self-organise its joint positions: `joint_targets` are pre-computed from the arithmetic progression and injected as a Gaussian source behind the PFR, and the bp/bp PIP fusion is hard-coded (L334-349, L364-373); the Turing dispersion is verified analytically, not as the pattern-selecting mechanism of the PDE | The poroelastic solver has a rigid solid skeleton (no u-p Biot displacement, effective stress, capsule or ligament), is 2D, one-way coupled (RD -> poroelastic), and its articular arch is a parametric Carter-Wong rule a(y) = A_arc phi(m)(1 - (y/W)^2), not a computed growth response; all constants are dimensionless and scaled only to adult cartilage | The vendored specimen is a juvenile hand radiograph with open physes, not an embryonic interzone section; the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd > mean; does_not_claim: A full Biot u-p or triphasic solution, 3D geometry, synovial fluid flow, capsule/ligament mechanics, convex-head emergence from growth (the model's head contour is flat because the lens cancels the arch), or any dimensional embryonic poroelastic constant." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1019-1023 and 1053 — Digit II's stored centerline has no bone contrast over its distal half (profile ~67 flat), so its DIP minimum is set by the window fraction, and `n_synovial_clefts: 3` is a constant. Re-trace the Digit II centerline through bone, detect the cleft count from the number of radiolucent minima with a contrast gate, and separate the joint space from the physis minimum 10-12 px distal (the specimen is juvenile).",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1598-1619 — the Sox9 reversion ratio and the loading threshold m* carry `reference_value: null`. Replace with a quantitative anchor (e.g. Kahn 2009 Fig. 4 Col2a1 signal in the muscle-less interzone, or Roddy 2011's graded immobilisation series) or move them out of the validation set into a 'predictions' list.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1872-1879 vs 1882 — `--m-load` / `--permeability` only reach `render_cavitation_figure`; Panel C of the comparison figure always uses m_load = 1 and 0. Thread the CLI values through `render_comparison_figure` and add a requirements lock file for the slot.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:334-349 and 364-373 — the 1D RD PDE places its interzones at pre-computed `joint_targets` injected as Gaussian `wave_drive` sources and hard-codes the Gdf5 bp/bp PIP fusion with `if cleft_amp < 0.35 and idx_j == 1: continue`. Replace the template with genuine wavelength selection (PFR-modulated D_G, D_N or kinetic parameters so the Turing wavelength of Law 2 sets the phalanx lengths) and let the bp/bp fusion follow from a Gdf5-dose-dependent cohesion/threshold.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:566-591 and 666 — A_arc_over_W = 0.22, K_identity = 0.30, kappa_G = 0.5, r_cav = 3.0 and the Kahn reversion factor 0.85 are uncited calibrations. Sweep A_arc and kappa_G (parameter-expressivity), and anchor at least kappa_G / sigma_0 to the Edwards 1994 / Maroudas 1976 ratio of interzone cohesion to Donnan pressure, or state them as free in the docstring and reference JSON.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:566-663 — the poroelastic solver is a storage equation with a rigid skeleton; add the solid displacement u and effective stress (Biot u-p, or at least a 1D consolidation column across the interzone) so that the tissue separation and the articular arch arise from strain, not from the parametric rule at L631-633.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:631-640 and 691-751 — the modelled proximal head contour is flat (head sagitta/half-span -0.036) because the Darcy lens thickens at the midline and cancels the imposed arch; the radiograph heads are convex. Either let the cavity reach the capsule periphery (Robin instead of Dirichlet drainage at the perichondrium) or compute the arch from a Carter-Wong growth law so a convex head / concave base pair emerges, and assert head_sagitta_norm > 0 in self-test check 12.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:869-948 — the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd 0.078 > mean 0.056. Add a second radiograph (adult, closed physes) or trace the MCP joints as well, and report a bootstrap CI so the model-specimen comparison in check 12 is not a 0.05 tolerance." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.94e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the 12-taxon morphospace and six genetic conditions are retained (L245-285, L951-982); Pass 3 adds two genuine mechanical parameters, each swept and monotone with a visible transition — muscle loading m_load (cavity count 0 -> 3 with threshold m* = 0.80, pore pressure monotone up, interzone Sox9 monotone down; L811-841) and Darcy permeability (cavity area monotone down, cavities lost at 16x; L844-866), both exposed on the CLI (`--m-load`, `--permeability`, L1863-1864) and rendered as Panels D-E. Deductions: A_arc_over_W, kappa_G, sigma_0 and beta_osm are not swept, so the articular arch amplitude and the cohesion threshold are fixed calibrations (-4); the loading sweep is coarse (9 points) and the threshold is reported to the grid resolution 0.2 (-2); the CLI `--m-load` and `--permeability` only affect the cavitation figure, not Panel C of the comparison figure (L1872-1879 vs L1882) (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — Reproducibility package: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `--self-test` runs 12 checks in 10.5 s including bitwise two-run determinism of both the RD PDE and the poroelastic solver (L1796-1804); the default invocation renders all three artifacts in 7.8 s; the explicit scheme carries a stability guard (L626-629); the audit environment (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0) is recorded; all dataset inputs are hash-verified. Deductions: no per-slot requirements lock file (-2); matplotlib needs a writable MPLCONFIGDIR and the script does not set one (-1); the GIF is not covered by a determinism check (-1); `measure_morphoeval()` re-runs every solver (16 metrics, ~9 s) rather than reading a cached run (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — Source and data traceability: 96/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: all 5 dataset files are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed on every run (L134-176); `synovial_cavitation_reference.json` records each Pass 3 source with DOI (or PMID for Edwards 1994), its finding, the reduced equations, dimensionless constants and a dimensional scaling note; the bib carries all 13 sources; the dataset README documents provenance and the juvenile-specimen caveat. Deductions: dimensional embryonic poroelastic constants are not available, only adult cartilage scales (Mow 1980, Maroudas 1976) are recorded (-2); Edwards 1994 has no DOI, PMID only (-1); the specimen's Wikimedia source is cited but its CC BY-SA attribution author is not recorded (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the comparison PNG shows the radiograph with traced centerlines and MCP/PIP/DIP markers beside the Kavanagh morphospace (Panels D, F), and the new Panel C / cavitation figure make the WT lens cavities, the paralysed uncavitated interzones and the Nog-/- rod visually distinct; the new joint-line arch trace agrees in sign with 3 of 4 valid joints (s/c 0.064 vs 0.056). Deductions: the specimen is a juvenile hand radiograph with open physes — the \"interzone clefts\" are adult joint spaces 10-12 px from a growth plate, not embryonic interzones (-5); Digit II's centerline has no bone contrast over its distal half (profile ~67 flat), so its DIP minimum is window-determined and it fails the Pass 3 contrast gate (L1019-1023) (-4); `n_synovial_clefts: 3` is asserted, not detected (L1053) (-3); the modelled proximal head contour is flat (head sagitta/half-span -0.036) because the lens thickening cancels the arch, whereas the radiograph heads are convex (-3); the joint-line statistic has sd 0.078 > mean 0.056 on n = 4 (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py L1019–L1023: PIP/DIP minima are argmin within hand-set window fractions; Digit II's distal profile has no bone contrast so its DIP is window-determined <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L1019-L1023>",
        "2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py L1053–L1053: `n_synovial_clefts: 3` is a constant, not a detection result <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L1053-L1053>",
        "datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/README.md L10–L10: Specimen is a juvenile radiograph with open physes (disclosed in Pass 3, not an embryonic interzone) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/README.md#L10-L10>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

