<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) Arithmetic Inhibitory Cascade Midpoint & One-Third Invariant Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that sequential inhibitory cascade segmentation constrains triphalangeal tetrapod digits to the exact affine line P_2 = (P_1 + P_3)/2 with middle phalanx occupying exactly 1/3 of total phalangeal length | Variables: P_1, P_2, P_3: proximal, middle, and distal phalanx lengths; A: distal mesenchymal activation; I: proximal condensation lateral inhibition; Δ = P_1(A - I)/I: cascade increment" ;
    dct:source "Kavanagh et al. (2013) PNAS 110(45):18190-18195 Figs. 1-2 & Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L130-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L28-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def phalanx_len (p1 delta n : Int) : Int :=
  p1 + (n - 1) * delta
def digit_total_3 (p1 delta : Int) : Int :=
  phalanx_len p1 delta 1 + phalanx_len p1 delta 2 + phalanx_len p1 delta 3
theorem kavanagh_inhibitory_cascade_midpoint_and_third (p1 delta : Int) :
    2 * phalanx_len p1 delta 2 = phalanx_len p1 delta 1 + phalanx_len p1 delta 3 ∧
    3 * phalanx_len p1 delta 2 = digit_total_3 p1 delta ∧
    phalanx_len 150 (-53) 2 = 97 ∧
    digit_total_3 150 (-53) = 291
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_n = P_1 [1 + (n-1)(A-I)/I] = P_1 + (n-1)Δ  ⇒  2 P_2 = P_1 + P_3,  P_2 / P_1 = 1/2 + (1/2)(P_3 / P_1),  3 P_2 = P_1 + P_2 + P_3" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.phalanx_len" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.kavanagh_inhibitory_cascade_midpoint_and_third" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hiscock et al. (2017) Distal PFR-FGF Tapering & BMP-GDF5-Noggin Turing Dispersion Sign Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes diffusion-driven Turing nucleation of periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ synovial joint interzones and strict proximal-to-distal phalanx tapering P_1 > P_2 > P_3 under a decaying distal PFR-FGF gradient | Variables: G: GDF5/Wnt9a synovial interzone activator; N: diffusible Noggin BMP antagonist; D_G, D_N: diffusion coefficients; q: spatial wavenumber; Δ < 0: distal PFR-FGF decay increment" ;
    dct:source "Hiscock, Tschopp & Tabin (2017) Dev. Cell 41:459-465; Hartmann & Tabin (2001) Cell 104:341-351" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L165-L340>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L57-L71> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gdf5_noggin_disp_det (f_G f_N g_G g_N D_G D_N q2 : Int) : Int :=
  (D_G * q2 - f_G) * (D_N * q2 - g_N) - f_N * g_G
theorem pfr_tapering_and_gdf5_noggin_turing_inversion (p1 delta : Int) (hd : delta ≤ -1) :
    phalanx_len p1 delta 1 > phalanx_len p1 delta 2 ∧
    phalanx_len p1 delta 2 > phalanx_len p1 delta 3 ∧
    (160 + (-210) : Int) = -50 ∧
    gdf5_noggin_disp_det 160 (-240) 190 (-210) 12 180 0 = 12000 ∧
    gdf5_noggin_disp_det 160 (-240) 190 (-210) 12 180 1 = -12120
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δ = P_1(A - I)/I < 0  ⇒  P_1 > P_2 > P_3;  Δ_disp(q^2) = (D_G q^2 - f_G)(D_N q^2 - g_N) - f_N g_G,  Δ_disp(0) > 0,  Δ_disp(q_c^2) < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.gdf5_noggin_disp_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.pfr_tapering_and_gdf5_noggin_turing_inversion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Brunet et al. (1998) & Storm et al. (1994) Noggin/Gdf5 Loss-of-Function Joint Cleft Ablation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why Noggin null (Nog-/-) embryos fail to repress BMP chondrogenesis in prospective interzones, abolishing all synovial joint clefts (N_joints = 0) into a single continuous cartilaginous rod, whereas Gdf5 brachypodism (bp/bp) selectively fuses proximal interphalangeal joints | Variables: nog_dose: Noggin BMP-antagonist dosage; gdf5_dose: GDF5 interzone signaling dosage; tau_cleft: chondrogenic repression threshold for synovial cavitation" ;
    dct:source "Brunet et al. (1998) Science 280:1455-1457; Storm et al. (1994) Nature 368:639-643" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L345-L490>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L82-L102> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def active_synovial_joints (nog_dose gdf5_dose tau_cleft : Nat) : Nat :=
  let amp := nog_dose * gdf5_dose
  if amp ≥ 3 * tau_cleft then 3
  else if amp ≥ 2 * tau_cleft then 2
  else if amp ≥ tau_cleft then 1
  else 0
theorem noggin_gdf5_joint_cleft_ablation (gdf5_dose : Nat) :
    active_synovial_joints 0 gdf5_dose 25 = 0 ∧
    segmented_phalanges 0 gdf5_dose 25 = 1 ∧
    active_synovial_joints 7 8 25 = 2 ∧
    active_synovial_joints 10 10 25 = 3 ∧
    segmented_phalanges 10 10 25 = 3
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Noggin = 0 (Nog-/-)  ⇒  N_joints = 0,  N_phalanges = 1 (continuous fused Sox9+ cartilage rod);  Gdf5 bp/bp  ⇒  PIP joint fusion (N_joints = 2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.active_synovial_joints" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.noggin_gdf5_joint_cleft_ablation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Reduced Biot Poroelastic Synovial Cavitation Gating Law (Mow 1980; Edwards 1994; Dowthwaite 1998; Drachman & Sokoloff 1966; Kahn 2009)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the two loss-of-function results the cavitation solver reproduces — paralysed / muscle-less embryos (m = 0) and Noggin-null embryos without interzones (G = 0) form no synovial cavity although the interzone may be specified — and that steady pore pressure is monotone in loading, which is why the --m-load sweep has a single cavitation threshold | Variables: G: Gdf5+ interzone identity (Hill transform of the RD Gdf5 field); H: hyaluronan; p: excess pore pressure; c: cavity phase field; m (Lean m_load): mechanosensitive loading gain φ(m_load) of embryonic muscle contraction; k_H, δ_H, D_H, S, κ_p, γ_osm, β_osm, σ_0, κ_G, r_c: dimensionless poroelastic constants (integers in hundredths in the Lean witnesses: β = k_H = 1, m = 10, G = 10, σ_0 = 100, κ = 5)" ;
    dct:source "Mow, Kuei, Lai & Armstrong (1980) J. Biomech. Eng. 102:73-84; Edwards et al. (1994) J. Anat. 185:355-367; Dowthwaite, Edwards & Pitsillides (1998) J. Histochem. Cytochem. 46:641-651; Drachman & Sokoloff (1966) Dev. Biol. 14:401-420; Kahn et al. (2009) Dev. Cell 16:734-743" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L556-L841>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L131-L158> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ha_steady (k_H m_load gdf5 : Nat) : Nat :=
  k_H * gdf5 * m_load
def pore_pressure_steady (beta k_H m_load gdf5 : Nat) : Nat :=
  beta * ha_steady k_H m_load gdf5
def interzone_cohesion (sigma_0 kappa gdf5 : Int) : Int :=
  sigma_0 - kappa * gdf5
def cavity_opens (p : Nat) (sigma_coh : Int) : Bool :=
  decide ((p : Int) > sigma_coh)
theorem poroelastic_cavitation_requires_load_and_interzone
    (beta k_H gdf5 m1 m2 : Nat) (sigma_coh : Int) (hpos : 0 < sigma_coh) (hm : m1 ≤ m2) :
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H 0 gdf5 = 0 ∧
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m1 0 = 0 ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady beta k_H 0 gdf5) sigma_coh = false ∧
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m1 gdf5 ≤ pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m2 gdf5 ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady 1 1 10 10) (interzone_cohesion 100 5 10) = true ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady 1 1 3 10) (interzone_cohesion 100 5 10) = false
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dH/dt = k_H φ(m) G − δ_H H + D_H ∇²H;  S ∂p/∂t = κ_p ∇²p + γ_osm (β_osm H − p), p = 0 at the perichondrium;  σ_coh = σ_0 (1 − κ_G G);  ∂c/∂t = r_c max(p − σ_coh, 0)(1 − c);  steady state p_ss = β_osm k_H φ(m) G / δ_H  ⇒  cavity iff p_ss > σ_coh;  m = 0 ∨ G = 0 ⇒ p_ss = 0 ⇒ no cavity;  m₁ ≤ m₂ ⇒ p_ss(m₁) ≤ p_ss(m₂)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.pore_pressure_steady" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.poroelastic_cavitation_requires_load_and_interzone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Darcy Lens-Cavity Midline Maximum Law (free perichondrial drainage; Mow 1980; Carter & Wong 1988)" ;
    dct:description "Explains the lens-shaped cavities of the solver (Panel A of joint_interzone_clefting_cavitation.png), the monotone loss of cavity area with permeability (Panel E), and — because the lens thickens on the midline — why the imposed articular arch does not yet produce a convex proximal head (carried as a Pass 4 item) | Variables: s: uniform osmotic fluid source across the interzone (β_osm H); κ: Darcy permeability; W: digit half-width; y: transverse coordinate; p: scaled steady pore pressure 2κp" ;
    dct:source "Mow, Kuei, Lai & Armstrong (1980) J. Biomech. Eng. 102:73-84; Carter & Wong (1988) J. Orthop. Res. 6:804-816; Roddy, Prendergast & Murphy (2011) PLoS ONE 6:e17526" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L566-L791>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L171-L193> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def darcy_lens_pressure (s W y : Int) : Int :=
  s * (W * W - y * y)
theorem darcy_lens_cavity_midline_maximum (s W y : Int) (hs : 0 ≤ s) :
    darcy_lens_pressure s W y ≤ darcy_lens_pressure s W 0 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure s W W = 0 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure 3 10 0 = 300 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure 3 10 6 = 192
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "κ p'' + s = 0 on [−W, W], p(±W) = 0  ⇒  2 κ p(y) = s (W² − y²);  s ≥ 0 ⇒ p(y) ≤ p(0) ∀y, p(±W) = 0  ⇒  the cavitation drive p − σ_coh is maximal on the digit midline and the cavity nucleates as a transverse lens" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.darcy_lens_pressure" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.darcy_lens_cavity_midline_maximum" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) Arithmetic Inhibitory Cascade Midpoint & One-Third Invariant Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that sequential inhibitory cascade segmentation constrains triphalangeal tetrapod digits to the exact affine line P_2 = (P_1 + P_3)/2 with middle phalanx occupying exactly 1/3 of total phalangeal length | Variables: P_1, P_2, P_3: proximal, middle, and distal phalanx lengths; A: distal mesenchymal activation; I: proximal condensation lateral inhibition; Δ = P_1(A - I)/I: cascade increment" ;
    dct:source "Kavanagh et al. (2013) PNAS 110(45):18190-18195 Figs. 1-2 & Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L130-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L28-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def phalanx_len (p1 delta n : Int) : Int :=
  p1 + (n - 1) * delta
def digit_total_3 (p1 delta : Int) : Int :=
  phalanx_len p1 delta 1 + phalanx_len p1 delta 2 + phalanx_len p1 delta 3
theorem kavanagh_inhibitory_cascade_midpoint_and_third (p1 delta : Int) :
    2 * phalanx_len p1 delta 2 = phalanx_len p1 delta 1 + phalanx_len p1 delta 3 ∧
    3 * phalanx_len p1 delta 2 = digit_total_3 p1 delta ∧
    phalanx_len 150 (-53) 2 = 97 ∧
    digit_total_3 150 (-53) = 291
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_n = P_1 [1 + (n-1)(A-I)/I] = P_1 + (n-1)Δ  ⇒  2 P_2 = P_1 + P_3,  P_2 / P_1 = 1/2 + (1/2)(P_3 / P_1),  3 P_2 = P_1 + P_2 + P_3" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.phalanx_len" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.kavanagh_inhibitory_cascade_midpoint_and_third" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hiscock et al. (2017) Distal PFR-FGF Tapering & BMP-GDF5-Noggin Turing Dispersion Sign Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes diffusion-driven Turing nucleation of periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ synovial joint interzones and strict proximal-to-distal phalanx tapering P_1 > P_2 > P_3 under a decaying distal PFR-FGF gradient | Variables: G: GDF5/Wnt9a synovial interzone activator; N: diffusible Noggin BMP antagonist; D_G, D_N: diffusion coefficients; q: spatial wavenumber; Δ < 0: distal PFR-FGF decay increment" ;
    dct:source "Hiscock, Tschopp & Tabin (2017) Dev. Cell 41:459-465; Hartmann & Tabin (2001) Cell 104:341-351" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L165-L340>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L57-L71> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gdf5_noggin_disp_det (f_G f_N g_G g_N D_G D_N q2 : Int) : Int :=
  (D_G * q2 - f_G) * (D_N * q2 - g_N) - f_N * g_G
theorem pfr_tapering_and_gdf5_noggin_turing_inversion (p1 delta : Int) (hd : delta ≤ -1) :
    phalanx_len p1 delta 1 > phalanx_len p1 delta 2 ∧
    phalanx_len p1 delta 2 > phalanx_len p1 delta 3 ∧
    (160 + (-210) : Int) = -50 ∧
    gdf5_noggin_disp_det 160 (-240) 190 (-210) 12 180 0 = 12000 ∧
    gdf5_noggin_disp_det 160 (-240) 190 (-210) 12 180 1 = -12120
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δ = P_1(A - I)/I < 0  ⇒  P_1 > P_2 > P_3;  Δ_disp(q^2) = (D_G q^2 - f_G)(D_N q^2 - g_N) - f_N g_G,  Δ_disp(0) > 0,  Δ_disp(q_c^2) < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.gdf5_noggin_disp_det" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.pfr_tapering_and_gdf5_noggin_turing_inversion" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Brunet et al. (1998) & Storm et al. (1994) Noggin/Gdf5 Loss-of-Function Joint Cleft Ablation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why Noggin null (Nog-/-) embryos fail to repress BMP chondrogenesis in prospective interzones, abolishing all synovial joint clefts (N_joints = 0) into a single continuous cartilaginous rod, whereas Gdf5 brachypodism (bp/bp) selectively fuses proximal interphalangeal joints | Variables: nog_dose: Noggin BMP-antagonist dosage; gdf5_dose: GDF5 interzone signaling dosage; tau_cleft: chondrogenic repression threshold for synovial cavitation" ;
    dct:source "Brunet et al. (1998) Science 280:1455-1457; Storm et al. (1994) Nature 368:639-643" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L345-L490>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L82-L102> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def active_synovial_joints (nog_dose gdf5_dose tau_cleft : Nat) : Nat :=
  let amp := nog_dose * gdf5_dose
  if amp ≥ 3 * tau_cleft then 3
  else if amp ≥ 2 * tau_cleft then 2
  else if amp ≥ tau_cleft then 1
  else 0
theorem noggin_gdf5_joint_cleft_ablation (gdf5_dose : Nat) :
    active_synovial_joints 0 gdf5_dose 25 = 0 ∧
    segmented_phalanges 0 gdf5_dose 25 = 1 ∧
    active_synovial_joints 7 8 25 = 2 ∧
    active_synovial_joints 10 10 25 = 3 ∧
    segmented_phalanges 10 10 25 = 3
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Noggin = 0 (Nog-/-)  ⇒  N_joints = 0,  N_phalanges = 1 (continuous fused Sox9+ cartilage rod);  Gdf5 bp/bp  ⇒  PIP joint fusion (N_joints = 2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.active_synovial_joints" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.noggin_gdf5_joint_cleft_ablation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Reduced Biot Poroelastic Synovial Cavitation Gating Law (Mow 1980; Edwards 1994; Dowthwaite 1998; Drachman & Sokoloff 1966; Kahn 2009)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the two loss-of-function results the cavitation solver reproduces — paralysed / muscle-less embryos (m = 0) and Noggin-null embryos without interzones (G = 0) form no synovial cavity although the interzone may be specified — and that steady pore pressure is monotone in loading, which is why the --m-load sweep has a single cavitation threshold | Variables: G: Gdf5+ interzone identity (Hill transform of the RD Gdf5 field); H: hyaluronan; p: excess pore pressure; c: cavity phase field; m (Lean m_load): mechanosensitive loading gain φ(m_load) of embryonic muscle contraction; k_H, δ_H, D_H, S, κ_p, γ_osm, β_osm, σ_0, κ_G, r_c: dimensionless poroelastic constants (integers in hundredths in the Lean witnesses: β = k_H = 1, m = 10, G = 10, σ_0 = 100, κ = 5)" ;
    dct:source "Mow, Kuei, Lai & Armstrong (1980) J. Biomech. Eng. 102:73-84; Edwards et al. (1994) J. Anat. 185:355-367; Dowthwaite, Edwards & Pitsillides (1998) J. Histochem. Cytochem. 46:641-651; Drachman & Sokoloff (1966) Dev. Biol. 14:401-420; Kahn et al. (2009) Dev. Cell 16:734-743" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L556-L841>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L131-L158> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ha_steady (k_H m_load gdf5 : Nat) : Nat :=
  k_H * gdf5 * m_load
def pore_pressure_steady (beta k_H m_load gdf5 : Nat) : Nat :=
  beta * ha_steady k_H m_load gdf5
def interzone_cohesion (sigma_0 kappa gdf5 : Int) : Int :=
  sigma_0 - kappa * gdf5
def cavity_opens (p : Nat) (sigma_coh : Int) : Bool :=
  decide ((p : Int) > sigma_coh)
theorem poroelastic_cavitation_requires_load_and_interzone
    (beta k_H gdf5 m1 m2 : Nat) (sigma_coh : Int) (hpos : 0 < sigma_coh) (hm : m1 ≤ m2) :
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H 0 gdf5 = 0 ∧
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m1 0 = 0 ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady beta k_H 0 gdf5) sigma_coh = false ∧
    pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m1 gdf5 ≤ pore_pressure_steady beta k_H m2 gdf5 ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady 1 1 10 10) (interzone_cohesion 100 5 10) = true ∧
    cavity_opens (pore_pressure_steady 1 1 3 10) (interzone_cohesion 100 5 10) = false
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dH/dt = k_H φ(m) G − δ_H H + D_H ∇²H;  S ∂p/∂t = κ_p ∇²p + γ_osm (β_osm H − p), p = 0 at the perichondrium;  σ_coh = σ_0 (1 − κ_G G);  ∂c/∂t = r_c max(p − σ_coh, 0)(1 − c);  steady state p_ss = β_osm k_H φ(m) G / δ_H  ⇒  cavity iff p_ss > σ_coh;  m = 0 ∨ G = 0 ⇒ p_ss = 0 ⇒ no cavity;  m₁ ≤ m₂ ⇒ p_ss(m₁) ≤ p_ss(m₂)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.pore_pressure_steady" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.poroelastic_cavitation_requires_load_and_interzone" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Darcy Lens-Cavity Midline Maximum Law (free perichondrial drainage; Mow 1980; Carter & Wong 1988)" ;
    dct:description "Explains the lens-shaped cavities of the solver (Panel A of joint_interzone_clefting_cavitation.png), the monotone loss of cavity area with permeability (Panel E), and — because the lens thickens on the midline — why the imposed articular arch does not yet produce a convex proximal head (carried as a Pass 4 item) | Variables: s: uniform osmotic fluid source across the interzone (β_osm H); κ: Darcy permeability; W: digit half-width; y: transverse coordinate; p: scaled steady pore pressure 2κp" ;
    dct:source "Mow, Kuei, Lai & Armstrong (1980) J. Biomech. Eng. 102:73-84; Carter & Wong (1988) J. Orthop. Res. 6:804-816; Roddy, Prendergast & Murphy (2011) PLoS ONE 6:e17526" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py#L566-L791>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_018_joint_interzone_clefting.lean#L171-L193> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def darcy_lens_pressure (s W y : Int) : Int :=
  s * (W * W - y * y)
theorem darcy_lens_cavity_midline_maximum (s W y : Int) (hs : 0 ≤ s) :
    darcy_lens_pressure s W y ≤ darcy_lens_pressure s W 0 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure s W W = 0 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure 3 10 0 = 300 ∧
    darcy_lens_pressure 3 10 6 = 192
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "κ p'' + s = 0 on [−W, W], p(±W) = 0  ⇒  2 κ p(y) = s (W² − y²);  s ≥ 0 ⇒ p(y) ≤ p(0) ∀y, p(±W) = 0  ⇒  the cavitation drive p − σ_coh is maximal on the digit midline and the cavity nucleates as a transverse lens" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jor.1100060604>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(66)90022-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00222-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.04.013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2017.04.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/260808a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/368639a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315213110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.3138202>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.280.5368.1455>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1177/002215549804600509>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017526> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled BMP-GDF5-Noggin Reaction-Diffusion Turing-Wavefront Synovial Joint Interzone Segmentation & Kavanagh (2013) Phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.darcy_lens_pressure" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_018.darcy_lens_cavity_midline_maximum" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

